  "implemented": [
    "BrowserEnrollmentKey generates Ed25519/ES256 nonextractable private keys, exports only raw public key for approval, restores structured-cloned CryptoKey pairs and verifies key-pair consistency.",
    "BrowserEnrollmentStore saves the complete normalized original request/key before backend approval in strict-durability IndexedDB transactions. Exclusive names and original-offer comparison prevent silently replacing intent or challenge. Issued bearer is never saved by the vault.",
    "BrowserEnrollmentSession signs the exact shared59byte JCS proof context. Fetch omits cookies, Authorization and explicit Origin, rejects redirects, uses no cache/referrer, bounds request/streamed response64KiB and includes signing/read/decode in one cancellation/deadline budget.",
    "Current exact Origin, offer/credential/issuer/installation/Device/Endpoint/key/transport/scope/recipient/absolute-expiry bindings are checked. Issued child bearer is memory-only for installation into exactly the approved transport, with independently supplied server signing and TLS trust.",
    "No implicit credential fallback across WT/WSS. Certificate pin input is bounded to8SHA256/32byte pins on WT, copied at installation and refused on WSS. Native storage-denial errors and server refusal messages are sanitized.",
    "Saved original recovery after reload does not regenerate IDs, keys or challenge. Rotation uses fresh name/original IDs/key; exact Device/Endpoint may be shared. Explicit local forgetting does not revoke server authority."
  ],
  "actual_browser_behavior": [
    "Four fresh client scenes: Ed25519/ES256 x WebTransport/WSS. Browser-generated key persists before approval; complete broader offer, duplicate original name, changed challenge and wrong transport installation refuse.",
    "All four fresh credentials open real signed peers through public enrollment.open. No operator/provider key or credential is passed to browser configuration.",
    "Four wrong Endpoint claims refuse before grant. Five genuine wrong-client-key WebCrypto proofs against a stolen challenge exhaust it, then the approved key also cannot grant.",
    "A second actual HTTPS Origin is separately listener-allowed. All four otherwise valid original signed claims refuse403 from that Origin, with no credential/Device/Endpoint/key effects.",
    "Wait beyond original challenge expiries, close the original browser target and fully restart server at identical contacts. A new target reloads IndexedDB original keys/offers, recovers the identical child ID/bearer hash/absolute expiry and opens all four peers. No issued bearer is supplied for recovery.",
    "Four expired pending challenges refuse gone on fresh proof; no grant rows are created. Four completed original claims recover after challenge expiry under current authority.",
    "Four fresh-key rotations retain exact Device/Endpoint. Revoking old enrollment refuses old claim recovery and actual signed peer. Replacement opens, then is independently revoked and refuses recovery. Eight credentials/eight keys/fourDevices/fourEndpoints total; no duplicate effects on replay."
  ],
  "trust_scope": "Owned temporary Chrome profile uses one synthetic leaf SPKI exception for HTTPS/WSS plus explicit short-lived WebTransport certificate hash. No system trust, personal browser profile, devices, account, provider or model execution. This is local functional qualification, not minimum-browser/performance/remote-network evidence.",
